\nReason:  \nThe best way to improve position and gain initiative is to develop space and prepare piece activity. Among the valid moves, **a2-a4** is safe, flexible, and prepares queenside expansion. It allows for future development of the bishop to b3 or c4, challenges Black’s potential b-pawn advances, and doesn’t weaken White’s structure. In contrast, h2-h4 is riskier and less urgent. Rook moves are too passive at this stage. b4-b5 is tempting but premature without more central control.\n\nAnswer: P: a2-a4"}
